                <pb facs="1525" n="1509" sameAs="frus:frus1949v06/pg1509"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>The General Assembly, at its Fourth Session, dealt with (1) the question of a
                    permanent international regime for the Jerusalem area and the protection of the
                    Holy Places and (2) the question of assistance to Palestinian refugees.</p>
                <p>The <hi rendition="#italic">Ad Hoc</hi> Political Committee of the Assembly
                    devoted 13 meetings to the first of these matters, from November 24 to 29 and
                    from December 5 to 7. The Committee’s proceedings during the earlier of these
                    periods are printed in United Nations, <hi rendition="#italic">Official Records
                        of the Fourth Session of the General Assembly, Ad Hoc Political Committee,
                        Summary Records of Meetings, 27 September–7 December 1949</hi> (hereinafter
                    identified as GA <hi rendition="#italic">4th sess., Ad Hoc Political
                        Committee</hi>), pages 246–306.</p>
                <p>Several proposals were offered to the Committee and on November 29, general
                    debate concluded, whereupon Subcommittee 1 was appointed to examine the
                    proposals (<hi rendition="#italic">ibid</hi>., page 305).</p>
            </div>
